sample outputs.\n\nNo maintainer-requested change or contributor-side blocker is pending from me. This note keeps the earlier ready claim visible after the newer same-issue PR submission.","createdAt":"2026-06-13T15:30:39Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4#issuecomment-4698955808","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABGCznyQ","author":{"login":"taherdhanera"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/claim #4\n\nVisibility refresh after the newer same-issue submission from @Deivid00007:\n- Newer issue activity: https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4#issuecomment-4700543132\n- Newer PR #2766: https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/pull/2766\n\nMy active earlier issue #4 submission remains PR #2281:\nhttps://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/pull/2281\n\nCurrent contributor-side status re-verified: PR #2281 is open, non-draft, CLEAN/mergeable, includes `/claim #4`, and closes #4. It remains the earlier Claude PR reviewer agent submission.\r\n","createdAt":"2026-06-14T03:21:02Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4#issuecomment-4700563401","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABGEQ74A","author":{"login":"boluo965"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-06-14T14:49:26Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4#issuecomment-4702092256","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABGEfhfw","author":{"login":"kish-00"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-06-14T16:17:23Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4#issuecomment-4702331263","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABGEgu3A","author":{"login":"taherdhanera"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/claim #4\n\nVisibility refresh after newer same-issue `/opire try` activity from @kish-00:\nhttps://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4#issuecomment-4702331263\n\nMy active earlier issue #4 submission remains PR #2281:\nhttps://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/pull/2281\n\nCurrent contributor-side state rechecked now:\n- PR #2281 is open and non-draft.\n- GitHub reports merge state `CLEAN` / mergeable.\n- PR body includes `/claim #4` and `Closes #4`.\n- Scope remains the completed Claude PR reviewer agent with CLI, Claude Code sub-agent instructions, GitHub Action, README/docs, tests, and real public PR sample outputs.\n\nNo maintainer-requested change or contributor-side blocker is pending from me.","createdAt":"2026-06-14T16:25:47Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4#issuecomment-4702351068","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABGEhxng","author":{"login":"daviediao-code"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-06-14T16:32:50Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4#issuecomment-4702368158","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABGEiUow","author":{"login":"daviediao-code"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire accept https://github.com/daviediao-code/claude-review-agent/tree/master","createdAt":"2026-06-14T16:36:38Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4#issuecomment-4702377123","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABGEiU3Q","author":{"login":"daviediao-code"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"## Submission\n\n**Repo:** https://github.com/daviediao-code/claude-review-agent/tree/master\n\n**What I built:**\n- CLI tool that fetches GitHub PR diffs and produces structured Markdown reviews\n- Summary of changes, identified risks, improvement suggestions, confidence score\n- Tested on real PRs (ytmusicapi#938, RustChain#7443) — sample outputs included in `sample_reviews.md`\n- Full README with setup and usage instructions\n\n**How to use:**\n```bash\n# Set your API key\nexport ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your-key-here\n\n# Review a PR\npython3 claude_review.py --pr https://github.com/sigma67/ytmusicapi/pull/938\n\n# Save to file\npython3 claude_review.py --pr https://github.com/sigma67/ytmusicapi/pull/938 --output review.md\n```\n\n**Sample review output on ytmusicapi#938:**\n```\n## Summary\nThis PR adds an optional `image: Path | None` parameter to `edit_playlist()` for setting custom playlist thumbnail images...\n\n## Identified Risks\n- Auth check is confusingly written: `if not self.auth_type == AuthType.BROWSER` uses double negation\n- No file size validation: Large files will consume bandwidth before failing\n- Code duplication: Resumable upload logic closely duplicates code in `uploads.py`\n\n## Improvement Suggestions\n- Extract shared `_resumable_upload()` helper into `_utils.py`\n- Add client-side file size validation (10MB limit)\n- Fix auth_type check to be more explicit\n\n## Confidence Score: High\n```\n\nThe agent correctly identifies code quality issues, security concerns, and provides actionable improvement suggestions.","createdAt":"2026-06-14T16:36:39Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4#issuecomment-4702377181","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABGEi0-g","author":{"login":"taherdhanera"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/claim #4\n\nFollow-up after newer same-issue external-repo activity from @daviediao-code:\n- `/opire try`: https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4#issuecomment-4702368158\n- `/opire accept` external repo: https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4#issuecomment-4702377123\n- submission note: https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4#issuecomment-4702377181\n\nMy active earlier target-repository issue #4 submission remains PR #2281:\nhttps://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/pull/2281\n\nCurrent contributor-side state rechecked now:\n- PR #2281 is open and non-draft.\n- GitHub reports merge state `CLEAN` / mergeable.\n- PR body includes `/claim #4` and `Closes #4`.\n- The implementation is already submitted inside this repository, with CLI, Claude Code sub-agent instructions, GitHub Action, README/docs, tests, and real public PR sample outputs.\n\nNo maintainer-requested change or contributor-side blocker is pending from me. This note keeps the earlier ready target-repo claim visible after the newer external-repo submission activity.","createdAt":"2026-06-14T16:40:00Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4#issuecomment-4702385402","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABGEmMFw","author":{"login":"Super-yueyue"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"I'll create a comprehensive PR review agent for Claude Code that analyzes pull requests and posts structured, actionable feedback.\n\n## PR Review Agent for Claude Code\n\n```javascript\n#!/usr/bin/env node\n\n/**\n * PR Review Agent for Claude Code\n * \n * Analyzes pull requests and posts structured, actionable feedback.\n * \n * Usage:\n *   node pr-review-agent.js --repo owner/repo --pr 123 [--gh-token YOUR_TOKEN]\n * \n * Environment variables:\n *   GITHUB_TOKEN - GitHub personal access token\n *   CLAUDE_API_KEY - Anthropic API key (optional, uses Claude Code's built-in if omitted)\n */\n\nconst fs = require('fs');\nconst path = require('path');\nconst https = require('https');\nconst { execSync } = require('child_process');\n\n// ─── Configuration ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nconst GITHUB_TOKEN = process.env.GITHUB_TOKEN || '';\nconst CLAUDE_API_KEY = process.env.CLAUDE_API_KEY || '';\n\n// Parse command line arguments\nconst args = process.argv.slice(2);\nconst repoArg = args.find(a => a.startsWith('--repo=')) || args[args.indexOf('--repo') + 1] || '';\nconst prArg = args.find(a => a.startsWith('--pr=')) || args[args.indexOf('--pr') + 1] || '';\nconst tokenArg = args.find(a => a.startsWith('--gh-token=')) || args[args.indexOf('--gh-token') + 1] || '';\n\nconst REPO = repoArg || (() => { console.error('Error: --repo is required (e.g., owner/repo)'); process.exit(1); })();\nconst PR_NUMBER = parseInt(prArg) || (() => { console.error('Error: --pr is required'); process.exit(1); })();\nconst FINAL_TOKEN = tokenArg || GITHUB_TOKEN;\n\nif (!FINAL_TOKEN) {\n  console.error('Error: GitHub token required. Set GITHUB_TOKEN env var or pass --gh-token');\n  process.exit(1);\n}\n\n// ─── GitHub API Helpers ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nfunction githubRequest(endpoint, method = 'GET', body = null) {\n  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n    const url = new URL(`https://api.github.com${endpoint}`);\n    const options = {\n      hostname: 'api.github.com',\n      path: url.pathname + url.search,\n      method,\n      headers: {\n        'Authorization': `Bearer ${FINAL_TOKEN}`,\n        'User-Agent': 'claude-code-pr-review-agent',\n        'Accept': 'application/vnd.github.v3+json',\n        'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n      },\n    };\n\n    const req = https.request(options, (res) => {\n      let data = '';\n      res.on('data', chunk => data += chunk);\n      res.on('end', () => {\n        try {\n          const parsed = JSON.parse(data);\n          if (res.statusCode >= 400) {\n            reject(new Error(`GitHub API error ${res.statusCode}: ${parsed.message || data}`));\n          } else {\n            resolve(parsed);\n          }\n        } catch (e) {\n          reject(new Error(`Failed to parse response: ${data.slice(0, 200)}`));\n        }\n      });\n    });\n\n    req.on('error', reject);\n    if (body) req.write(JSON.stringify(body));\n    req.end();\n  });\n}\n\n// ─── Fetch PR Data ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nasync function fetchPRData() {\n  console.log(`🔍 Fetching PR #${PR_NUMBER} from ${REPO}...`);\n\n  const [pr, files, comments, reviewComments] = await Promise.all([\n    githubRequest(`/repos/${REPO}/pulls/${PR_NUMBER}`),\n    githubRequest(`/repos/${REPO}/pulls/${PR_NUMBER}/files`),\n    githubRequest(`/repos/${REPO}/issues/${PR_NUMBER}/comments`),\n    githubRequest(`/repos/${REPO}/pulls/${PR_NUMBER}/comments`),\n  ]);\n\n  return { pr, files, comments, reviewComments };\n}\n\n// ─── Analyze with Claude ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nasync function analyzeWithClaude(prData) {\n  const { pr, files } = prData;\n\n  console.log('🧠 Analyzing PR with Claude...');\n\n  // Build file summaries\n  const fileSummaries = files.map(f => ({\n    filename: f.filename,\n    status: f.status,\n    additions: f.additions,\n    deletions: f.deletions,\n    patch: f.patch ? f.patch.slice(0, 3000) : null, // Truncate for token limits\n    changes: f.changes,\n  }));\n\n  const prompt = `You are a senior software engineer reviewing a pull request. Provide a structured, actionable review.\n\nPR Title: ${pr.title}\nPR Description: ${pr.body || '(no description)'}\nAuthor: ${pr.user.login}\nBranch: ${pr.head.ref} → ${pr.base.ref}\nTotal Files Changed: ${files.length}\nTotal Changes: +${files.reduce((s, f) => s + f.additions, 0)} / -${files.reduce((s, f) => s + f.deletions, 0)}\n\n## Changed Files\n${fileSummaries.map(f => `\n### ${f.filename} (${f.status})\n+${f.additions} / -${f.deletions}\n${f.patch ? `\\`\\`\\`diff\\n${f.patch}\\n\\`\\`\\`` : '(binary or large file)'}\n`).join('\\n---\\n')}\n\n## Review Guidelines\n- Identify potential bugs, security issues, and logic errors\n- Check for code quality, readability, and maintainability issues\n- Suggest improvements with specific code examples\n- Verify adherence to common best practices\n- Consider edge cases and error handling\n- Check for hardcoded values, magic numbers, or security vulnerabilities\n\n## Output Format\nProvide your review as a structured JSON object with this exact format:\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Overall summary of the PR (2-3 sentences)\",\n  \"score\": \"1-10 rating (10 = perfect, 1 = needs major rework)\",\n  \"approve\": true/false,\n  \"issues\": [\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"critical\" | \"major\" | \"minor\" | \"suggestion\",\n      \"file\": \"filename\",\n      \"line\": null or line number,\n      \"title\": \"Short issue title\",\n      \"description\": \"Detailed explanation with code examples if applicable\",\n      \"suggestion\": \"How to fix or improve\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"strengths\": [\"List of positive aspects\"],\n  \"action_items\": [\"Actionable next steps for the author\"]\n}`;\n\n  // Use Claude Code's built-in analysis if available, otherwise make API call\n  if (CLAUDE_API_KEY) {\n    return await callClaudeAPI(prompt);\n  } else {\n    return await callClaudeCodeCLI(prompt);\n  }\n}\n\nasync function callClaudeAPI(prompt) {\n  const response = await fetch('https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages', {\n    method: 'POST',\n    headers: {\n      'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n      'x-api-key': CLAUDE_API_KEY,\n      'anthropic-version': '2023-06-01',\n    },\n    body: JSON.stringify({\n      model: 'claude-3-opus-20240229',\n      max_tokens: 4000,\n      messages: [{ role: 'user', content: prompt }],\n    }),\n  });\n\n  const data = await response.json();\n  const content = data.content?.[0]?.text;\n  \n  // Extract JSON from response\n  const jsonMatch = content.match(/\\{[\\s\\S]*\\}/);\n  if (!jsonMatch) throw new Error('No JSON found in Claude response');\n  \n  return JSON.parse(jsonMatch[0]);\n}\n\nasync function callClaudeCodeCLI(prompt) {\n  try {\n    const result = execSync(\n      `echo ${JSON.stringify(prompt)} | claude -p \"Analyze this PR review context and output ONLY valid JSON matching the specified format:\"`,\n      { encoding: 'utf-8', maxBuffer: 10 * 1024 * 1024 }\n    );\n    \n    const jsonMatch = result.match(/\\{[\\s\\S]*\\}/);\n    if (!jsonMatch) throw new Error('No JSON found in Claude CLI response');\n    \n    return JSON.parse(jsonMatch[0]);\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error('Claude CLI error:', error.message);\n    // Fallback to a basic analysis\n    return generateBasicReview(prompt);\n  }\n}\n\n// ─── Fallback Analysis ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nfunction generateBasicReview(_prompt) {\n  console.log('⚠️ Using fallback analysis...');\n  return {\n    summary: \"Automated review complete. For detailed analysis, ensure Claude API key is configured.\",\n    score: 5,\n    approve: false,\n    issues: [],\n    strengths: [\"PR structure appears standard\"],\n    action_items: [\"Run with CLAUDE_API_KEY for detailed analysis\"]\n  };\n}\n\n// ─── Post Review Comment ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nasync function postReview(prData, reviewResult) {\n  console.log('📝 Posting review comment...');\n\n  const { pr } = prData;\n  const { summary, score, approve, issues, strengths, action_items } = reviewResult;\n\n  // Build emoji indicators\n  const scoreEmoji = score >= 8 ? '🟢' : score >= 5 ? '🟡' : '🔴';\n  const approveEmoji = approve ? '✅' : '❌';\n\n  // Build issues section\n  const issuesSection = issues.map((issue, i) => {\n    const severityEmoji = {\n      'critical': '🔴',\n      'major': '🟠',\n      'minor': '🟡',\n      'suggestion': '💡',\n    }[issue.severity] || '⚪';\n\n    const fileLine = issue.file ? `**File:** \\`${issue.file}\\`` + (issue.line ? ` (line ${issue.line})` : '') : '';\n    \n    return `${severityEmoji} **${issue.severity.toUpperCase()}:** ${issue.title}\n${fileLine}\n${issue.description}\n${issue.suggestion ? `> **Suggestion:** ${issue.suggestion}` : ''}\n`;\n  }).join('\\n');\n\n  // Build strengths section\n  const strengthsSection = strengths.map(s => `- ✅ ${s}`).join('\\n');\n\n  // Build action items\n  const actionsSection = action_items.map(a => `- [ ] ${a}`).join('\\n');\n\n  const commentBody = `## 🤖 Claude Code PR Review\n\n### Summary\n${summary}\n\n### Score: ${scoreEmoji} ${score}/10 | **${approveEmoji} ${approve ? 'Approve' : 'Changes Requested'}**\n\n---\n\n### ${issues.length > 0 ? '🔍 Issues Found' : '✅ No Issues Found'}\n${issues.length > 0 ? issuesSection : 'No issues detected in this review.'}\n\n---\n\n### 💪 Strengths\n${strengthsSection || 'No specific strengths noted.'}\n\n---\n\n### 📋 Action Items\n${actionsSection || 'No specific action items.'}\n\n---\n\n<sub>Review generated by Claude Code PR Agent | Score: ${score}/10</sub>`;\n\n  // Post as PR review or issue comment\n  const endpoint = `/repos/${REPO}/issues/${PR_NUMBER}/comments`;\n  await githubRequest(endpoint, 'POST', { body: commentBody });\n\n  console.log('✅ Review posted successfully!');\n  return commentBody;\n}\n\n// ─── Main Execution ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nasync function main() {\n  console.log('🚀 Starting PR Review Agent...');\n  console.log(`📂 Repository: ${REPO}`);\n  console.log(`🔢 PR Number: ${PR_NUMBER}`);\n\n  try {\n    // Step 1: Fetch PR data\n    const prData = await fetchPRData();\n    console.log(`📄 Found ${prData.files.length} changed files`);\n\n    // Step 2: Analyze with Claude\n    const reviewResult = await analyzeWithClaude(prData);\n    console.log(`📊 Review score: ${reviewResult.score}/10`);\n\n    // Step 3: Post structured review\n    const comment = await postReview(prData, reviewResult);\n\n    // Step 4: Output results\n    console.log('\\n📋 Review Summary:');\n    console.log(comment);\n\n    // Exit with appropriate code\n    process.exit(reviewResult.approve ? 0 : 1);\n\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error('❌ Error during review:', error.message);\n    process.exit(2);\n  }\n}\n\nmain();\n```\n\n## Package Configuration\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"claude-code-pr-review-agent\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"description\": \"AI-powered PR review agent using Claude Code\",\n  \"main\": \"pr-review-agent.js\",\n  \"bin\": {\n    \"pr-review\": \"./pr-review-agent.js\"\n  },\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"review\": \"node pr-review-agent.js\",\n    \"start\": \"node pr-review-agent.js\"\n  },\n  \"keywords\": [\"claude\", \"code-review\", \"pr-review\", \"github\"],\n  \"license\": \"MIT\"\n}\n```\n\n## GitHub Actions Workflow\n\n```yaml\n# .github/workflows/pr-review.yml\nname: Claude Code PR Review\n\non:\n  pull_request:\n    types: [opened, synchronize, reopened]\n\njobs:\n  review:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    permissions:\n      contents: read\n      pull-requests: write\n      issues: write\n    \n    steps:\n      - name: Checkout code\n        uses: actions/checkout@v4\n        with:\n          fetch-depth: 0\n\n      - name: Setup Node.js\n        uses: actions/setup-node@v4\n        with:\n          node-version: '20'\n\n      - name: Install dependencies\n        run: npm install\n\n      - name: Run PR Review Agent\n        env:\n          GITHUB_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}\n          CLAUDE_API_KEY: ${{ secrets.CLAUDE_API_KEY }}\n        run: |\n          node pr-review-agent.js \\\n            --repo=${{ github.repository }} \\\n            --pr=${{ github.event.pull_request.number }}\n```\n\n## Usage Examples\n\n### Basic Usage\n```bash\n# Using environment variable\nexport GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_xxxxx\nexport CLAUDE_API_KEY=sk-ant-xxxxx\n\nnode pr-review-agent.js --repo=owner/repo --pr=42\n```\n\n### With CLI Arguments\n```bash\nnode pr-review-agent.js \\\n  --repo=owner/repo \\\n  --pr=42 \\\n  --gh-token=ghp_xxxxx\n```\n\n### Docker Support\n```dockerfile\nFROM node:20-alpine\n\nWORKDIR /app\nCOPY package.json pr-review-agent.js ./\nRUN npm install\n\nENTRYPOINT [\"node\", \"pr-review-agent.js\"]\n```\n\n## Key Features\n\n1. **Structured Review Format**: Issues categorized by severity (critical, major, minor, suggestion)\n2. **Actionable Feedback**: Specific code examples and improvement suggestions\n3. **Scoring System**: 1-10 rating with clear approval/rejection\n4. **GitHub Integration**: Fetches PR data and posts comments automatically\n5. **Fallback Analysis**: Works even without Claude API key\n6. **Emoji-rich Output**: Visual indicators for quick scanning\n7. **Exit Codes**: 0 for approve, 1 for reject, 2 for errors\n8. **CI/CD Ready**: GitHub Actions workflow included\n\nThe agent provides comprehensive, structured reviews that help developers quickly understand what needs attention and how to fix issues, making code review more efficient and consistent.","createdAt":"2026-06-14T17:02:04Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4#issuecomment-4702440471","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABGEnDsw","author":{"login":"taherdhanera"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/claim #4\n\nFollow-up after newer same-issue inline submission activity from @Super-yueyue:\n- latest issue comment: https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4#issuecomment-4702440471\n\nMy active earlier target-repository issue #4 submission remains PR #2281:\nhttps://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/pull/2281\n\nCurrent contributor-side state rechecked in this monitoring pass:\n- PR #2281 is open and non-draft.\n- GitHub reports it `MERGEABLE` / `CLEAN`.\n- PR body includes `/claim #4` and `Closes #4`.\n- The implementation is submitted in this repository and includes the CLI, Claude Code sub-agent instructions, GitHub Action, README/docs, tests, and real public PR sample outputs.\n\nNo maintainer-requested change or contributor-side blocker is pending from me. This note keeps the earlier ready in-repo claim visible after the newer inline issue submission.","createdAt":"2026-06-14T17:07:38Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4#issuecomment-4702454707","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABGG7toA","author":{"login":"5AIBountyHunter"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try\n\nI'll build a Claude Code sub-agent that reviews PR diffs and posts structured comments. Working on it now — PR incoming.\n\nThe agent will support:\n- CLI: \\claude-review --pr <url>\\\n- GitHub Action workflow included\n- Structured output: summary, risks, suggestions, confidence score\n- Tested on real GitHub PRs","createdAt":"2026-06-15T05:38:10Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4#issuecomment-4704890272","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABGG9GkA","author":{"login":"taherdhanera"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/claim #4\n\nStatus refresh after the latest same-issue `/opire try` activity:\n- latest issue comment: https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4#issuecomment-4704890272\n\nMy earlier in-repository issue #4 submission remains PR #2281:\nhttps://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/pull/2281\n\nCurrent c